{"archetypes":[{"name":"scope-anchor-flow","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff threads a staged scope anchor through many plan-review, voter, revise, and result-env paths where one missed handoff can silently reintroduce stale scope.","prompt_body":"Trace SCOPE_ANCHOR_FILE and feature-file flow across plan-review-loop, run-step3-review, dispatch-plan-review-panel, dispatch-plan-voters, revise-plan-with-waterfall, lib-phase-driver, and SKILL.md handoff logic. Look for stale IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR fallback, non-staged anchor paths, missing CR/LF sanitation, early-exit paths that drop the value, or callers that still use brainstorm-merged context as binding scope. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"scope-marker","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new leading [SCOPE-REDUCTION] marker must survive collect, dedup, aggregation, and tally without changing vote thresholds.","prompt_body":"Investigate check-scope-reduction-marker, lib-vote-tally integration, plan-review dedup, collect fixtures, and tally behavior for tagged findings. Verify leading-only detection, severity-prefix normalization, fenced and inline false negatives, non-leading false negatives, no special OOS behavior, and unchanged neutral or rejected vote outcomes. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"aggregation-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan-mode aggregation now splits tagged findings from LLM merging and renumbers combined output, which is a high-risk transformation path.","prompt_body":"Review aggregate-findings.sh and its harnesses for the plan-mode split, untagged-only merge prompt, tagged-block append, marker/reviewer parity validation, fallback behavior, and final sequential renumbering. Check whether validation failures restore the correct in-scope input rather than pre-split files, whether temp files are cleaned safely, and whether duplicate headings can still reach ballots. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"prompt-boundary","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Multiple prompts inline untrusted issue or scope text, creating injection and delimiter-handling risk beyond ordinary code security review.","prompt_body":"Inspect reviewer, voter, revise, scout, and MainAgent prompt changes for robust untrusted-evidence framing around issue and scope-anchor content. Pay special attention to delimiter escaping, redaction behavior, XML-like tag injection, malicious closing tags, and whether any path tells agents to treat anchor text as instructions rather than evidence. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The implementation adds several shell helpers and inline Python snippets where macOS Bash 3.2, BSD utilities, and set -e interactions commonly cause latent failures.","prompt_body":"Review new and modified shell scripts for Bash 3.2 compatibility, POSIX/BSD utility assumptions, quoting, arrays, pipelines under set -euo pipefail, subshell variable scope, and tempfile cleanup. Include plan-block-strip-body, check-scope-reduction-marker, render-voter-prompt, compute-pr-line-counts, render-run-summary, and the larger plan-review-loop and aggregate-findings edits where relevant. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"reporting-metrics","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff includes PR line-count and final-report changes outside the core scope-anchor flow that need targeted integration review.","prompt_body":"Examine compute-pr-line-counts, render-run-summary, write-final-report, related tests, and Makefile registration for correctness and integration with existing run-summary and PR-report contracts. Look for parsing mismatches, missing degraded-mode behavior, brittle git diff assumptions, or output changes that could break downstream consumers. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
